            "output": "<path>C:\\Users\\Flavi\\opencode\\IIGC\\experiments\\common_basis\\cross_transfer\\README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Cross-transfer kappa matrix\n2: \n3: Train mode x test mode on the same SAC actor parameters, same two-deal\n4: rollout protocol, only the (train, test) mode pairing changes.\n5: \n6: Matrix (reinforce field, mean over seeds 41-44):\n7: \n8: | train \\ test | single | dynamic |\n9: |--------------|--------|---------|\n10: | single       | 0.402 ± 0.085 | 0.518 ± 0.044 |\n11: | dynamic      | 0.487 ± 0.074 | 0.477 ± 0.027 |\n12: \n13: awr: all cells ~0.50 (0.500/0.508, 0.499/0.533).\n14: softq: 0.566/0.524, 0.596/0.542.  expq: 0.562/0.517, 0.581/0.520.\n15: \n16: ## Interpretation\n17: \n18: - The predicted \"unadapted policy contracts under hidden relations\"\n19:   (kappa(S->D) < kappa(S->S)) is NOT observed: kappa(S->D) = 0.518 >\n20:   kappa(S->S) = 0.402.\n21: - Coherent alternative pattern: **cross-transfer RAISES reinforce kappa in\n22:   both test modes** (D->S > S->S and S->D > D->D). A mismatched policy behaves\n23:   homogeneously regardless of deal (uniformly low-skill play), so its\n24:   return-weighted gradients agree more across deals; a matched policy's\n25:   performance varies with the deal, so its gradients disagree more. The\n26:   reinforce field is dominated by return variance in this protocol.\n27: - softq/expq show the reverse (in-mode higher), and awr is flat at ~0.50.\n28: \n29: ## Protocol limitation\n30: \n31: Each rollout is a *mixture* of assignments (the hidden team depends on the\n32: random deal, and 30 episodes span many different teams). kappa between two\n33: random mixtures measures cross-deal agreement, not a clean\n34: relation-conditioned contrast. The decisive refinement is to FORCE one\n35: assignment per rollout (fix the red-A holder per deal) and compare\n36: assignment A vs assignment B directly.\n37: \n38: Run: `python experiments/common_basis/cross_transfer/run_cross_transfer.py`\n39: Results: `data/kappa/cross_transfer/results.json`\n\n(End of file - total 39 lines)\n</content>",
